#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199307} :activity/id #uuid "31aab6dd-2cc2-5648-88d8-e57c688c618a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049016 :topic/id #uuid "d40c7f73-0923-5b33-8a87-c53afe20cdeb" :topic/math-academy-id 4158} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199271 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198371 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198013 :question/id #uuid "c8dd9065-9db8-53da-b6a5-cf6cddd3a3e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-11675"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c38eccf8-9941-58de-888c-c44130ed48da" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050605}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198960} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198968} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281466} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281467} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281478} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281638}] :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Repeated Integral as a Mixed Integral"} :step/id #uuid "2ecadc5e-e56f-5cb0-8a78-a7a91da258bd" :step/math-academy-id 43193 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199272}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199272 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198372 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198014 :question/id #uuid "83df52ed-139b-5dff-8b32-942aafeff0ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-11676"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e87509d-95fe-5804-a94b-d42ada81e4f7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198967} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198971} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281479} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281482} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281483} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365192} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365199} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372055} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389312}] :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration in a Triple Integral"} :step/id #uuid "08180a9a-2473-5b5c-bf97-d2ef2156c578" :step/math-academy-id 43194 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199310}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199307 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199474 :tutorial/content "Consider the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\n\\int_0^1 \\int_0^{1-x} \\int_0^{1-x-y} f(x,y,z) \\:\\textrm{d}z\\:\\textrm{d}y\\:\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFor this repeated integral, the integration domain is the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1-x, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1-x-y \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/56/56ef205e4a92cf96d2ddb81635b5776ededf880d4507e68db1d66ae045533705.png)\n\nSuppose we wish to change the order of integration so that we integrate first with respect to $y,$ then over a region $D$ in the $xz$-plane. In other words, we wish to express our repeated integral in the form\n\n$$\n\\int_0^1 \\int_0^{1-x} \\int_0^{1-x-y} f(x,y,z) \\:\\textrm{d}z\\:\\textrm{d}y\\:\\textrm{d}x\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left[ \\int_{u_1(x,z)}^{u_2(x,z)} f(x,y,z) \\:\\textrm{d}y \\right] \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\textrm{d}z\\:\\textrm{d}y\\:\\textrm{d}x$ to $\\textrm{d}y\\:\\textrm{d}A,$ we write $R$ as a type III region. \n\nTo visualize $R$ as a type III region, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/3c/3c444ce37b1799e950b52789d7837b699938bec602e274fed7c91640a31812a2.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the back boundary and leaves through the front boundary:\n\n- The front boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nz = 1-x-y,\n$$\n\nand writing this in the form $y = u_2(x,z),$ we have\n\n$$\ny = 1-x-z.\n$$\n\n- The back boundary of the region is $y = 0.$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is \n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,z) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1-x-z \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/31/31c74e0c21a02898e584d141e942037cedf392680b9bc3bd84ae8831fb55224c.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration so that it is integrated first with respect to $y$ and then over $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "b266db14-83cd-503a-9a9a-0a046db8b914" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7667 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4ef19e30-5711-5c99-9378-bdff12e2c640" :step/math-academy-id 44543 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199271}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199310 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198396 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198038 :question/id #uuid "15684778-4ac6-5741-b17b-4ba9f8a193e4" :question/math-academy-id "e-12405"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1eaf02c-e29b-58dd-aa24-8b0bb70183a0" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198969} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198970} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281480} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281481} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326734} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365185} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365206} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366104}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral by Swapping the Order of Integration"} :step/id #uuid "bdf0c9c2-cbc5-5ca4-8248-c9b49ffdbda4" :step/math-academy-id 44564}] :activity/title "Changing the Order of Integration in Triple Integrals: Changing Region" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198491}]}
